# The inputs of the static pacman that scripts/build-pacman-static builds.
#
# Each record pins one input by content: a tarball by sha256, pacman by
# commit. The static pacman is a release asset. ⛔ The Dockerfile does not read
# this file, and no image build fetches anything named here.
#
# Records, one per line, fields separated by white space:
#
#   zig       VERSION  HOST  URL  SHA256
#   source    NAME  VERSION  URL  SHA256
#   mirror =  NAME  URL
#   pacman    COMMIT  URL
#   describe  VALUE
#   tag       NAME  TAG-OBJECT-SHA
#   signer    FINGERPRINT  NAME
#   keyserver URL
#
# A mirror line gives one more URL for the record NAME. NAME is the name of a
# source record, or zig-HOST for a zig record. The build tries the URL of the
# record first, then each mirror line of that record in file order.
#
# ⭐ The sha256 is the trust anchor, not the host. The build keeps a download
# only when its sha256 equals the pin. A download with a different sha256 is
# deleted, and the build tries the next URL. When no URL gives the pinned
# bytes, the build stops.
#
# ⛔ Add a mirror line only after you measure the same sha256 at that URL:
#   curl -sSfL --connect-timeout 20 --max-time 900 -o f URL && sha256sum f
#
# A mirror on distfiles.gentoo.org uses a directory of two hex digits. The two
# digits are the start of the BLAKE2B hash of the file name:
#   python3 -I -c 'import hashlib,sys; print(hashlib.blake2b(sys.argv[1].encode()).hexdigest()[:2])' FILE
#
# docs/measurements.md gives the date of each measurement.

#---------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# The toolchain.
#
# zig is the C compiler, the linker, the archiver and the musl source in one
# download. One zig cross compiles to every port from one host. The build
# picks the record whose HOST is the host it runs on.
#---------------------------------------------------------------------------#
zig 0.16.0 x86_64-linux https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/zig-x86_64-linux-0.16.0.tar.xz 70e49664a74374b48b51e6f3fdfbf437f6395d42509050588bd49abe52ba3d00
zig 0.16.0 aarch64-linux https://ziglang.org/download/0.16.0/zig-aarch64-linux-0.16.0.tar.xz ea4b09bfb22ec6f6c6ceac57ab63efb6b46e17ab08d21f69f3a48b38e1534f17
mirror = zig-x86_64-linux https://pkg.hexops.org/zig/zig-x86_64-linux-0.16.0.tar.xz
mirror = zig-x86_64-linux https://zig.linus.dev/zig/zig-x86_64-linux-0.16.0.tar.xz
mirror = zig-x86_64-linux https://fs.liujiacai.net/zigbuilds/zig-x86_64-linux-0.16.0.tar.xz
mirror = zig-aarch64-linux https://pkg.hexops.org/zig/zig-aarch64-linux-0.16.0.tar.xz
mirror = zig-aarch64-linux https://zig.linus.dev/zig/zig-aarch64-linux-0.16.0.tar.xz
mirror = zig-aarch64-linux https://fs.liujiacai.net/zigbuilds/zig-aarch64-linux-0.16.0.tar.xz

#---------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# The static libraries, in the order the build makes them.
#
# scripts/build-pacman-static has one build function per source record, and
# it builds the records in this order. tests/static/85-pacman-static-pin.sh
# checks that each record has its function.
#
# ⚠ curl has no brotli and no nghttp2. The binary uses HTTP/1.1 and does not
# accept the br content encoding. An Arch mirror needs neither. brotli does not
# compile for loongarch64 with zig cc.
#
# ⚠ OpenSSL is the 3.5 long term support line.
#---------------------------------------------------------------------------#
