#---------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# pacman.
#
# ⭐ The commit is the commit of the pacman that the images ship. The anchor
# tag family is <alias>-<describe>-<pkgrel>. The describe value ends in g and
# the start of this commit. tests/static/85-pacman-static-pin.sh checks that
# the two agree. The freshness workflow compares describe with the live anchor.
#
# ⛔ Pin the commit, not the tag. The build checks out the commit. The tag can
# point at an older commit than the one Arch ships.
#
# The tag line pins the signed release tag by its object sha, because a tag
# name can move. The build fetches that tag object and checks its signature.
# ⚠ The signature covers the tagged commit. The commits between the tag and the
# pinned commit have no signature. The commit sha covers them.
#
# The signer lines name the keys that may sign the tag. The fingerprint is the
# identity. The name is a label for the reader. The public key of each signer
# is in keys/<FINGERPRINT>.asc. The build imports that file first. It tries the
# keyservers, in file order, only when the file does not give the key.
#
# ⛔ The build checks the fingerprint of each key it imports, from any source.
# It requires a VALIDSIG whose primary key fingerprint is a signer line.
#
# To export a key file again:
#   gpg --keyserver hkps://keyserver.ubuntu.com --recv-keys FINGERPRINT
#   gpg --armor --export-options export-minimal --export FINGERPRINT > keys/FINGERPRINT.asc
#---------------------------------------------------------------------------#
pacman 54d94116164b0b2202c6061c4a59c6f3e70820d8 https://gitlab.archlinux.org/pacman/pacman.git
describe 7.1.0.r9.g54d9411
tag v7.1.0 208ff2b57e49f2851ce7bca5ac9090c6cb8aa746
signer 6645B0A8C7005E78DB1D7864F99FFE0FEAE999BD Allan McRae
signer B8151B117037781095514CA7BBDFFC92306B1121 Andrew Gregory
keyserver hkps://keyserver.ubuntu.com
keyserver hkps://pgpkeys.eu
